course: dictionary
lesson: 4276
title: Greatly: very much
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Greatly means very much, or to a large amount. It tells you how big a change or a feeling is. «A helmet greatly lowers the chance of a serious head injury.» The helmet makes the chance much smaller, not just a little smaller.
explain: Greatly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. It often goes with verbs such as improve, increase, reduce and appreciate. «James Watt greatly improved the steam engine» means he made it much better.
explain: You will often see greatly in formal writing and reports, where people want to describe big changes clearly. Read the words around it to check the size of the change. Ask yourself: is the change big or small?
fact: Greatly means very much or to a large amount.
fact: Greatly is an adverb, so it describes how an action happens.
fact: Phrases you may see include «greatly improved», «greatly reduced» and «greatly appreciated».
fact: «Root hairs greatly increase the surface for taking in water.» Here greatly shows the surface gets a lot bigger.
fact: Greatly is often used in formal writing and reports.
exercise: «A helmet greatly lowers the chance of a serious head injury.» What does greatly mean here? | Not at all | *A lot, by a large amount | Quickly | A little bit
exercise: Ella says greatly means a little, so «greatly improved» only means a tiny bit better. Is she right? | Yes, but only in reports | No, greatly means very much, so it means a big improvement | *Yes, greatly always means a little | No, greatly means very slowly
exercise: «The Ming greatly extended the walls.» Which word tells you how big the extending was? | Ming | extended | *greatly | walls
test: «Her help was greatly appreciated by the whole class.» What does greatly show? | That her help was small and nobody noticed | *That her help was valued very much | That the class was late | That she was help
test: «The US government greatly increased deportations, and there were protests.» What does greatly tell you about the increase? | *It was a very small increase | It was a very large increase | It happened at the seaside | There was no increase
exam: «The new path greatly reduced the time to school.» Which choice means the same as greatly reduced? | Made much shorter | *Cut down by a large amount | Made much longer | Made into a river
